 "spin_named": "One-cushion cannon; the caption names no spin. Subtitles: 'ho ho, look at this for a shot', 'wow'.",
 "spin_inferred": "Top (follow), hit very hard, and no side that shows. The blue is struck almost full (2 to 4 degrees of cut): the cue ball is left with 0.6 m/s at heading 70-75, then speeds up and bends forward as the top spin bites, reaching a steady 1.04 m/s at heading 47 some 0.6 s after contact (acceleration about 1.7 m/s2, roughly along the aim line). That is less top than a rolling ball carries: a ball rolling at 7.3 m/s would follow through at about 2 m/s, so the spin at contact was about half of natural roll. At the left-hand side cushion it comes in 46.9 degrees off the cushion and leaves 43.7 off it, having lost about 40 % of its speed both along the cushion (0.71 to 0.45 m/s) and into it (0.76 to 0.43): nothing there says running or check side with any confidence.",
